<article class="env-proposition" id="E98A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/E98A">Proposition <span data-tag="E98A">2.1.4.8</span>.</a> The category $(\sSet )_{/S}$ is a simplicial model category $($with respect to the covariant model structure and the natural simplicial structure$)$. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We will deduce this from Proposition <a href="/tag/420A" data-tag="420A">8.3.1.7</a>. The only nontrivial point is to verify that for any $X \in (\sSet )_{/S}$, the projection $X \times \Delta ^ n \rightarrow X$ is a covariant equivalence. But this map has a section $X \times \{ 0\}  \rightarrow X \times \Delta ^ n$, which is left anodyne and therefore a covariant equivalence (Proposition <a href="/tag/9D6B" data-tag="9D6B">2.1.4.9</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>